<!--
  sce:std/mesh/causal_entry.scxml — one entry of a causal route's version
  vector (docs/adr/0085, sections 3 and 3.3): a replica of the group and a
  number among that replica's changes. A list of these is a vector: the
  delivered vector of a copy, the context a change is tagged with, the vector
  a `causalVector` carries, and the stable cut. An entry also names one change,
  its dot: the replica that authored it and its number, from 1 with no gap.

  The replica is its 16-byte UUID v7 as two halves, its first eight bytes and
  its last eight, each read big-endian, as envelope_id holds an envelope id:
  a record's fields are fixed-width scalars, and two identities compare as
  their byte strings do.

  The envelope carries a vector under key 20 (`causal_vector`), the sender's
  own entry first.

  replica 0001...0f, its third change → hi 0x0001020304050607,
  lo 0x08090a0b0c0d0e0f, seq 3.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="causal_entry"
       sce:event-name="mesh.causal_entry">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="hi" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="lo" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="seq" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
